# Dashboard v3's BUILT output. The Dockerfile builds cbedge-v3 inside the image
# and, on success, does `rm -rf public/v3 && cp -r cbedge-v3/dist public/v3`.
#
# That v3 build step is deliberately non-fatal, so a v3 failure can never block a
# v2 hotfix — and the else branch says "/v3 will 404 until this is fixed."
#
# It did not 404. public/v3 used to be COMMITTED, so a failed build simply left
# the last committed copy in place and the VPS served it. On 2026-09-12 that was
# a build from 2026-08-29: three weeks stale, silently, with git in sync on both
# machines and nothing in any log to say so. The old bundle predated the 48-col /
# 8px-row board grid, so it rendered a current-units layout at the old 32px row
# height and every card came out ~4x too tall — "all the cards are super
# stretched out", which is not a board bug at all.
#
# Untracked, the failure is loud again: no fallback, /v3 404s, and a broken v3
# build is visible the moment it happens instead of three weeks later.
public/v3
